{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552531-watcher-valeren-sense-cycle-confuses-me-can-someone-explain-it","id":1552531,"title":"Watcher Valeren Sense Cycle confuses me can someone explain it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-19T11:47:29-07:00","id":1552531,"title":"Watcher Valeren Sense Cycle confuses me can someone explain it?","content":"We had no intentions of splat when started this game as a human we wanted to see where it led and it led to vtm(it's a single player game the ST is my wife and she had ideas for multiple splats and I had no idea what I wanted play as it had been years since I'd touched the hobby)<br /> <br /> As we settled on splat she jokingly suggested salubri and specifically Watcher Valeren. She says she had never seen it used in play and wanted to see how it worked I read it and thought I understood it. The passive effect is easy enough, but the questions youre aloud to ask seem vague to the point it hurts my head and as written there are few examples of said questions enough to make it more confusing as to what it does. Is this ST dependant or is there an intended way its meant to be used? Is there more material that helps explain this stuff anywhere and how exactly it functions and what questions apply in regards to its use? As it is now I default to a specific set of questions in game that the ST has ruled work , but the ST has said 'get creative we are testing this let's see how far we can go'(btw I'm fully in on this I want to see what this BS can do its passive power alone makes me chuckle ), but without really understanding this I'm lost as to how to 'get creative' .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27499-singlebodyriot","name":"SingleBodyRiot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T15:11:09-07:00","id":1552554,"title":"","content":"Not sure if I should specify that I mean from V20..I completely forgot to mention edition and I'm not sure what all this is in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27499-singlebodyriot","name":"SingleBodyRiot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T17:00:37-07:00","id":1552557,"title":"","content":"You can ask virtually anything, and at most the ST will have to determine how many successes the question uses, although it should be noted that even a single success can answer a lot. The only limitation is that you must ask something about the target specifically, not something just tangentially related to the target.<br /> <br /> Ask the target position, ask their Backgrounds, their relationship to another character or position, if they're hostile or amicable to someone else (remember that immediate hostility towards you is already covered by the passive effect). It's hard to give many examples not because it's restrictive, but because the possibilities are too broad.<br /> <br /> It is quite a powerful effect as far as information gathering goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_